         "master_id": 77243,
         "master_url": "https://api.discogs.com/masters/77243",
         "title": "Conspiracy Of One",
         "country": "Europe",
         "released": "2000",
         "notes": "Track 14 is an unlisted bonus track. The included CD-text lists it as \"Huck It\".\n\nReleased in a standard jewel case with clear tray and 16-page booklet.\n\nSome copies have a red/black sticker which reads:\nCONTAINS ORIGINAL PRANKSTER, MILLION MILES AWAY & BONUS TRACK HUCK IT (FROM THE FILM 'HUCK IT')\nPARENTAL ADVISORY EXPLICIT LYRICS\n4984812008\nN/S\n\nOn some copies, the sticker's bottom two lines read:\n4984812006\nD\n\nEnhanced content on the sampler disc is a custom media player, made with Macromedia Projector, that can show/play four included music videos, karaoke versions of two songs from the album (with optional vocal tracks), and a sneak peek at the upcoming \"Huck It\" DVD/Video. All videos are also accessible directly on the disc in Quicktime MOV-format, but the vocal tracks for the karaoke songs can't be accessed. Also included is a weblink to The Offspring Nation Fanclub's website. \n\nRecorded at NRG, North Hollywood, CA \nMixed at Southern Tracks, Atlanta, GA \nMastered at Oasis Mastering, Studio City, CA \n\nRedman appears courtesy of Def Jam Records. \n\n\"Intro\" performed by [a372789] from \"[m271003]\", under license from Sabucat Productions \n\"Original Prankster\" contains portions of \"[m=153087]\", as performed by [a9707], used courtesy of Far Out Productions, Inc./Avenue Records.\n\"Special Delivery\" contains portions of [a258997]'s \"[m=302149]\", used by permission of EMI Svenska AB. Written by [a565289], courtesy of Screengems-EMI Music, Inc./BMI.\n\nCD-text logo is printed on the disc \n\n\"Pretty Fly (For A White Guy)\" music video © 1998 Sony Music Entertainment Inc.\n\"Why Don't You Get A Job\", \"The Kids Aren't Alright\" and \"She's Got Issues\" music videos © 1999 Sony Music Entertainment Inc.\n\nAll Songs © 2000 Underachiever Music (BMI), administered by King, Purtich, Holmes, Paterno & Berliner, LLP in the US and Canada\nRecording ©℗ 2000 Sony Music Entertainment Inc.\nMade in Austria",
         "released_formatted": "2000",
