         "master_id": 77234,
         "master_url": "https://api.discogs.com/masters/77234",
         "title": "Americana",
         "country": "Europe",
         "released": "1998",
         "notes": "Track 13 contains a hidden track that begins at the 9:16 mark, preceded by (approx.) 1:05 of silence\n\nTrack 4 contains a sample from \"Rock Of Ages\", Def Lepp Music (Administered by Zomba Enterprises, Inc.)/Zomba Enterprises (ASCAP)\n\nRecorded and mixed at Eldorado Recording Studio, Burbank, CA \nMastered at Oasis Mastering, Studio City, CA \n\nJim Lindberg and Jack Grisham appear courtesy of Epitaph Records\nDavey Havoc appears courtesy of Nitro Records\n\nAll songs © 1998 Underachiever Music (BMI) admin. by Wixen Music Publishing, Inc. (BMI). Except \"Feelings\" © 1974 Fermata International Melodies Inc./Loving Guitar Music Inc. (ASCAP)\n©℗ 1998 Sony Music Entertainment Inc. \nDistribution Sony Music\nMade in Austria\n\nReleased in standard jewel case with clear tray and including a 16-page full colour booklet with lyrics, credits and artwork. Copies known where the rear of the original jewel case has a moulded 'Sony Music' on the lower left corner, embossed on the inside.\n\nInitial copies came with round red sticker on front stating \"Contains the single \"Pretty Fly (For A White Guy)\" See them on tour in January and February across Europe - 01-491656-10\"\n\nSome copies came with a round red sticker on the jewel case stating: \"Includes the singles Pretty Fly (For A White Guy)\" and \"Why Don't You Get A Job?\" 01-491656-10\"\n\nSome later copies had a red sticker on the jewel case stating: \"Includes the singles \"Pretty Fly (For A White Guy)\", \"Why Don't You Get A Job\", \"The Kids Aren't Alright\" & \"She's Got Issues\" - 4916562002\"\n\nRoss Garfield Of [url=https://www.discogs.com/artist/929979-Drum-Doctors]Drum Doctor[/url]",
         "released_formatted": "1998",
