         "lowest_price": 4.79,
         "master_id": 17107,
         "master_url": "https://api.discogs.com/masters/17107",
         "title": "Mind The Gap (Deluxe) (CD 2)",
         "country": "Germany",
         "released": "2004-11-08",
         "notes": "- This is german release of this deluxe edition with tracks 6 & 13 tagged as bonus tracks and besided videoclip + photos there is also additional interview and making of document as multimedia part. Booklet has got merchandise and adverts pages.\n- Comes in a 2CD-Jewelcase housed in a cardboard box, including a 2-sided poster.\n\n---\n\nTracks 1-1, 1-4, 1-6, 1-8, 1-11 to 1-13, 2-12 published by Warner/Chappel / Hanseatic.\nTrack 1-2 published by Elstak Music / Corbeau Music Publishing B.V. / Warner/Chappel / Hanseatic.\nTrack 1-3 published by Harrick Music Inc. / EMI Longitude Music / Warner/Chappel / Hanseatic. Contains music of \"Shake Your Booty\" (Casey/Finch).\nTrack 1-5 published by WB Music Corp. (ASCAP) Warner-Tamerlane Pub. Corp. / Old Crow Music (BMI) / Ignorant Music (ASCAP) / Zen Of Iniquity, admin. by Almo Music Corp. (ASCAP) / WB Music Corp. / Canvas Mattress Music (ASCAP) / Universal Music Publ. / Neue Welt Musikverlag / Sony-ATV-Music Publ.\nTrack 1-7 published by Universal Music Publishing.\nTrack 1-9 published by EMI Music Publishing Ltd. Assigned by Grabbing Hands Music.\nTrack 1-10 published Sony ATV Discos Music Publishing.\nTrack 2-2 published by Loop Dance Constructions Musikverlag GmbH / Hanseatic / Planet Phuture / Warner/Chappel.\nTrack 2-3 published by Nanada Music / Warner/Chappel / Hanseatic.\nTracks 2-4 to 2-7, 2-9, 2-10 published by Loop Dance Constructions Musikverlag GmbH / Warner/Chappel / Hanseatic.\nTrack 2-8 published by Edition Get Into Magic c/o Warner/Chappel.\nTrack 2-11 published by Edition 2000 / Red Rooster / BMG.\nTrack 2-13 published by Rückbank Musikverlage.\n\nTrack 1-3 & 1-10: sample replay production by Mark Summers for Scorccio Music Replay\nThis is an analogue recording. All tracks have been produced, performed & programmed by Scooter for Sheffield Tunes Communications. Made at Loop D. C. Studios 1 and 2, Europe, Hamburg, Bramfeld.\n\nMultimediapart: Video: Marc Schoelermann, Melanie Mohr, Michael Menke (evermotion). Interview & making of: Oliver Franke (Berlinièros). Photos: Mathias Bothor, Jan Schwede\n\nMassive shout out to the crowd! Find out what you cannot do and then go and do it!\n\nCD2 recorded live in Hamburg during the 'We Like It Loud Tour 2004' at the docks\n\n℗&© 2004 Sheffield Tunes.\nDistribution: Edel Distribution GmbH.\nPrinted and manufactured in Germany by optimal.\n\nFront stickers:\n2CD CD + Bonus CD\nIncl. Top-Hits Shake That!\n+ One (Always Hardcore)\n+ Stripped + All I Wanna Do\n+ 2-sided poster\n+ 2 Bonustracks\n+ Special Multimedia-Part\nfeat. Video, Making of, Photos + Interview\nBonus Live CD\nfeat. 13 (!) selected live essentials\n\nDELUXE\n- Album CD\n- Bonus CD (feat. 13 live tracks)\n+ 2 Bonustracks\n+ Poster + Video\n+ Making Of + Photos\n+ Interview",
         "released_formatted": "08 Nov 2004",
