         "master_url": "https://api.discogs.com/masters/78103",
         "title": "Fantasy",
         "country": "US",
         "released": "1995-09-12",
         "notes": "(Tracks #2 and #3 are NOT identical. Track #3 is the remix most people are familiar with. This version completely omits the chorus from the album version and substitutes the bridge from the album version instead. Track #2 is structured similarly, but appends the first two instances of the bridge with the original chorus from the album version. The original chorus occurs at approximately 1:24 and 2:19.)\n\n[Published by] Sony Songs Inc. / Rye Songs (BMI) / Metered Music, Inc. / WB Music Corp. / Stone Jam Publishing / Ness, Nitty And Capone Inc. (ASCAP). All rights on behalf of Rye Songs administered by Sony Music Publishing. All rights on behalf of Metered Music, Inc. administered in the U.S. and Canada by Polygram International Publishing, Inc. \"Fantasy\" contains a sample of \"[url=http://www.discogs.com/Tom-Tom-Club-Genius-Of-Love/master/90477]Genius Of Love[/url]\" performed by [a48404]. Used courtesy of Warner Bros. Records, Island Records and Metered Music. Produced for Untouchables Entertainment. Recorded at The Hit Factory, New York City. Mastered [at] Gateway Mastering, Portland, Maine.\n\nTracks 2 to 4 remix produced for Bad Boy Entertainment Inc. Recorded at The Hit Factory, New York City. Mixed at The Hit Factory, New York City. Mastered at The Hit Factory, New York City.\n\nTrack 5 remix produced for Def Mix Productions. Additional production and arrangement for Def Mix Productions. Mastered at The Hit Factory, New York City. Music recorded and mixed at Quad Studios, New York City.\n\nSpecial mixes taken from the forthcoming Columbia release \"[url=http://www.discogs.com/Mariah-Carey-Daydream/master/78027]Daydream[/url]\" (66700). In store Tuesday, October 3.\n\n© 1995 Sony Music Entertainment Inc. ℗ 1995 Sony Music Entertainment Inc. Manufactured by Columbia Records.\n\nSome copies came with a circular hype sticker.",
         "released_formatted": "12 Sep 1995",
